From d8b95cbd4c07a2bbbcee1f25933e31e504c86ebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:32:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 286: leaving one mention visible is a copying task, not
 a weighing one

The smoke ran entirely in a degenerate regime and every gate in it was
measuring nothing. At --min-mentions 2 an address holds two mentions;
hiding one leaves one, so the candidate list had a single entry - n_cands
was 1 at every logged step - and the only choice left was that value or
UNKNOWN. The model learned to answer the only candidate, scored 0.875 by
doing so, and never abstained once.

The lying tape collapsed the same way. It forges one visible mention, and
with a single mention visible that is the entire record replaced rather
than a lie among evidence. Model and votes both scored -1.0 because
nothing survived to contradict the forgery.

So an address must be able to spare a mention and still hold a
comparison: --min-evidence, default 2, is how many mentions stay visible,
and examples that cannot meet it are refused rather than scored. The lie
is refused below two visible mentions for the same reason.

And a gate before the gates. G_task_exists requires at least twenty
leave-one-out examples, more than one candidate on average, and some
target the visible evidence genuinely cannot supply; NO_TASK is the
overall verdict when it fails, so a degenerate run says so instead of
reporting numbers about a copying exercise. Verified on a hand tape:
two mentions are refused, three give a real two-candidate choice, hiding
a lone minority value yields target UNKNOWN, and the forgery now leaves
votes tied where the corroboration feature still separates.

